WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.475
Mateo: “I support the queue, but I don’t know when to use Assign versus Transfer.” A short, role-specific demonstration followed by a worked example targets Knowledge.

00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:14.619
Ask Mateo to explain which action fits a sample ticket and why.

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:17.314
Nia: “I can explain every step.

00:00:17.554 --> 00:00:27.581
In the evening shift my account cannot assign tickets, and I have no cover to practice.” Another slide deck will not fix the permission problem or create practice time.

00:00:27.821 --> 00:00:34.071
Help resolve authorized access through the proper support route, then provide protected practice and feedback.

00:00:34.311 --> 00:00:36.082
These conditions block Ability.

00:00:36.772 --> 00:00:42.063
The difference is the evidence: being able to explain a task is not the same as completing it.

00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:43.903
Observed performance matters.

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:47.513
These are fictional cases, not Prosci assessment items.

00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:54.027
Original worked practice: give Mateo a sample ticket with no owner and an unresolved question.

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:57.851
Demonstrate assigning an owner and writing a next action once.

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:00.886
Then let Mateo complete a new ticket without hints.

00:01:01.126 --> 00:01:09.041
If the explanation is accurate but the action fails, ask what happened and inspect the environment before prescribing more instruction.

00:01:09.731 --> 00:01:15.811
Consider accessibility: the practice route should work with the tools and accommodations the person needs.

00:01:16.051 --> 00:01:18.611
A system obstacle is not a character flaw.

00:01:19.301 --> 00:01:20.389
Now it's your turn.

00:01:20.629 --> 00:01:24.810
Nia explains the steps correctly but her account cannot assign tickets.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.311
Choose the most useful immediate response.

00:01:27.551 --> 00:01:30.666
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

